translated_text:
HEAD OF DPPAS KAB. BELITUNG
CHAPTER IV
FORMS OF VIOLENCE
Article 5
Forms of violence against women and children include: a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. neglect;
e. coercion/deprivation of liberty;
f. exploitation;
g. threat of certain actions; and/or
h. other violence.

text:
BAB V
HAK PEREMPUAN DAN ANAK KORBAN TINDAK KEKERASAN
Pasal 6
Perempuan dan anak korban tindak kekerasan mendapatkan  hak sebagai berikut:
a. hak untuk dihormati harkat dan martabat sebagai manusia; b. hak atas pemulihan kesehatan dan psikologis dari  penderitaan yang dialami korban;
c. hak menentukan sendiri keputusannya;
d. hak mendapatkan informasi;
e. hak atas kerahasiaan;
f. hak atas kompensasi;
g. hak atas rehabilitasi sosial;
h. hak atas penanganan pengaduan;
i. hak korban dan keluarganya untuk mendapatkan kemudahan  dalam proses peradilan; dan
j. hak atas pendampingan.

translated_text:
CHAPTER V
RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 6
Women and children victims of acts of violence shall receive the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected;
b. the right to recovery of health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by the victim;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality;
f. the right to compensation;
g. the right to social rehabilitation;
h. the right to complaint handling;
i. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process; and
j. the right to assistance.

