translated_text:
Article 17
(1) The forms of services provided to women and children victims of acts of violence are as follows:
a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. legal assistance;
d. rehabilitation and social reintegration;
e. repatriation;
f. identification services; and
g. psychological services.
(2) Services as referred to in paragraph (1) must be supported by facilities in the form of:
a. special service rooms within the police force;
b. expert and professional personnel;
c. service centers and safe houses; and/or
d. other facilities and infrastructure necessary for victim recovery.
(3) The forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in accordance with minimum service standards established by the government and implemented by related OPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. women's empowerment and child protection; and
d. mental and spiritual.
(4) In carrying out the duties and functions as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government cooperates with government agencies, other regional governments, non-governmental organizations, and social institutions.
(5) Further provisions regarding the procedures for handling services for women and children from acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), paragraph (2) and paragraph (3), shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

text:
Pasal 23
Selain membentuk PPT dalam Perlindungan Perempuan dan  Anak sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 22, guna menunjang  terlaksananya penyelenggaraan perlindungan kepada perempuan  dan anak dari tindak kekerasan, dibentuk:
a. Gugus tugas tindak pidana perdagangan orang;
b. Komite aksi daerah penghapusan bentuk-bentuk pekerjaan  terburuk untuk anak;
c. Gugus tugas perlindungan perempuan dan anak tingkat  kecamatan;
d. Kelompok pencegahan kekerasan dalam rumah tangga tingkat  kelurahan/desa; dan
e. Bentuk tugas lainnya yang menunjang Pusat Pelayanan  Terpadu Dalam Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak.

translated_text:
Article 23
In addition to establishing the PPT in the Protection of Women and Children as referred to in Article 22, in order to support the implementation of protection for women and children from acts of violence, the following shall be established:
a. Task force on criminal acts of human trafficking;
b. Regional action committee for the elimination of the worst forms of child labor;
c. Sub-district level task force for the protection of women and children;
d. Domestic violence prevention groups at the village/sub-village level; and
e. Other forms of task forces that support the Integrated Service Center for the Protection of Women and Children.

text:
Pasal 24
