Article 28
(1) In order to achieve the objectives of protection of women and children from acts of violence as referred to in Article 3, the Regional Government cooperates with:
a. the Government;
b. the Provincial Government;
c. other Regency/City Governments; and
d. non-governmental institutions.
(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1), includes:
a. provision of data and information;
b. rehabilitation of victims of acts of violence;
c. repatriation and social reintegration; and
d. provision of evidence and witnesses;
(3) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

CHAPTER XIII
GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION
Article 31
(1) Regional Government is obligated to conduct guidance and supervision of the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence.
(2) Guidance as referred to in paragraph (1), includes: a. guidelines and fulfillment standards;
b. technical guidance and training;
c. provision of facilities;
d. monitoring; and
e. evaluation.
(3) Guidance as referred to in paragraph (2), in the framework of realizing the objectives of protection of the rights of women and children from acts of violence in accordance with minimum service standards implemented by OPD/related agencies and the community.

CHAPTER XIV
FINANCING
Article 34
Financing for the implementation of protection of women's and children's rights from acts of violence is sourced from:
a. State Revenue and Expenditure Budget;
b. Provincial Regional Revenue and Expenditure Budget;
c. Regional Revenue and Expenditure Budget (APBD);
d. Village Revenue and Expenditure Budget; and
e. Other legal and non-binding financial sources in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
